The invention relates to a trimming device (2) and associated method for trimming hooves of animals. The trimming device according to the invention comprises
- a platform (50) on which an animal for trimming can be positioned and which is provided with an entrance (6) and an exit (14);
- a number of uprights (56, 72) connected to the platform;
- a number of girders () connected to at least some of the uprights; and
- at least one lifting mechanism for lifting a leg of the animal for trimming, wherein the material for at least a part of the platform, the uprights and the girders is substantially a lightweight material comprising a number of profiled elements.

The invention relates to a steel alloy comprising, in percent by mass:
- 0.17 to 0.23 carbon;
- 1.40 to 1.60 silicon;
- 0.50 to 0.60 manganese;
- up to 0.020 phosphor;
- up to 0.020 sulfur;
- up to 0.30 chrome;
- up to 0.12 molybdenum;
- up to 0.80 nickel;
- up to 0.30 copper;
- up to 0.03 vanadium;
the remainder being iron and incidental impurities.

A method for nucleic acid sequencing comprising:
delivering sequencing reagents to a sequencing chip, wherein the sequencing chip comprises an array of reaction cells, one or more waveguides, and an array of detectors, wherein the array of reaction cells are configured to receive the sequencing reagents;
delivering illumination light to the one or more waveguides of the sequencing chip to illuminate the sequencing reagents in the array of reaction cells, thereby generating emission light;
transmitting the emission light from the array of reaction cells to the array of detectors, wherein the emission light from the respective reaction cell in the array of reaction cells is directed to a corresponding detector in the array of detectors;
converting the emission light received by the array of detectors into electrical data signals;
performing pre-processing of the data in the data signals using circuits on the sequencing chip; and
transferring the pre-processed data to a processor off of the sequencing chip for downstream processing, wherein the sequencing chip is integrated such that the emission light from the array of reaction cells is transmitted to the array of detectors without passing through air or free space.

A process for treating wastewater or sewage comprising:
receiving a wastewater inflow or a sewage inflow in a first reactor (100A);
receiving an outflow from the first reactor (100A) to one or more second reactors;
receiving an outflow from the one or more second reactors in a nitritation reactor (100B);
receiving an overflow (230) of partially treated wastewater or partially treated sewage from the nitritation reactor (100B) in an anammox reactor (110);
receiving a bypass flow from the first reactor (100A) and/or the one or more second reactors in the anammox reactor (110);
receiving a mixed liquor flow from the anammox reactor (110) into one or more clarifiers (120A, 120B), wherein if there are more than one clarifiers, the clarifiers are connected in parallel;
providing a first return activated sludge flow from the clarifier (120A, 120B) to the first reactor;
providing a second return activated sludge from the clarifier (120A, 120B) to the nitritation reactor (100B);
providing a third return activated sludge flow from the clarifier (120A, 120B) to the anammox reactor (110); and,
optionally blending the overflow from the nitritation reactor (100B) and the bypass flow from the first flow reactor (100A) in the anammox reactor (110),
wherein the first reactor (100A) and the one or more second flow equalization reactors are each separated by a partition wall (180), and
wherein the partition wall(s) comprise one or more openings providing fluid communication therethrough.

The invention relates to a Fluid-bed granulator system for producing fertilizer granules with a defined size at least comprising:
a.) a fluid-bed granulator (1)
b.) a first cooler (2) externally connected with the fluid-bed granulator (1) or forming an internal part of the fluid-bed granulator (1),
c.) a product screen (3) connected with the first cooler (2) wherein the product screen (3) at least comprises:
- an exit for on-size particles (3a);
- an exit for oversized particles (3b) and
- an exit for undersized particles (3c);
c.1) wherein the exit for undersized particles (3c) is connected with the fluid-bed granulator (1) and wherein the exit for oversized particles (3b) is connected with the fluid-bed granulator (1) via one or more crushers (4);
c.2) wherein the exit for on-size particles (3a) is connected with a first splitter (5a) and wherein the first splitter (5a) is connected with the fluid-bed granulator (1) and a post processing unit (22); and
wherein a particle size analyzer (24) is located between the fluid-bed granulator (1) and the product screen (3).

The invention concerns a method for controlling a hybrid power generation plant connected to a grid, said plant comprising a hydro plant, having a power-efficiency curve including a forbidden zone in which instability can occur, and one or more among a solar plant and a battery storage system, said method comprising :
- reducing or increasing the power produced by the hydro plant so that it operates outside its forbidden zone;
- and increasing or reducing the power produced by the solar plant and/or the battery storage system, so that the whole power produced by the hybrid power generation plant stays constant or corresponds to the requirement of the grid.

The present invention relates to a dryer (10) comprising:
• a casing (12) including a basement (13);
• a laundry chamber (14) suitable to receive laundry to be dried;
• a process air circuit for circulating process air into said laundry chamber (14);
• a condensing device (22) for removing moisture from the process air coming from said laundry chamber (14) located within the process air circuit;
• a water collecting housing (30) for the collection of moisture condensed by said condensing device (22);
• a condensate tank (36) to collect water transferred from the water collecting housing (30);
• a pump unit (44) associated to said water collecting housing (30) for the removal of water contained therein and to pump it to the condensate tank (36);
• a first conduit (50) fluidly connecting a pump unit outlet (45) to a condensate tank inlet (37);
• a second conduit (60) fluidly connecting the condensate tank (36) to an inlet opening (23) arranged in the basement (13); and
• wherein the dryer (10) also includes a siphon-like element (52, 62) located in the first and/or in the second conduit (50, 60) to limit air transfer through the first and/or second conduit (50, 60).The present invention also relates to a method for production of a dryer (10).
